On 6/15/07, m.kornig@sondal.net <m.kornig@sondal.net> wrote:
>
> What about names? Doesn't the stress rule
> (stress last but one syllable) apply to them as
> well??

That's the most common way of pronouncing them, but it is not
required for unambiguous parsing. No matter where you stress it,
a cmevla cannot be confused with any other word. You can even stress
it in more than one syllable if it's a long cmevla, or not stress it at all
if it's a short one.

